From 292bee6f15b94a4b179c105050d5fdaed58d5e76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:18:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm_moe_dsa: prompt attention through msa2 on BF16 576-wide
 rows

Mia's AI Lab's msa2 kernel (their GLM-5.3 recipe, patches 0150 / 0158 /
0162; Apache-2.0) ported from its FP8 / FP4 latent caches with a separate
rope cache to this engine's interleaved BF16 rows: one block a prompt
row, the rank's heads one m16 tile, each warp loading its own 128 latent
and 16 rope columns of a 16-key tile one tile ahead, warp-order score
sums, online softmax, P V straight to the output (no partials, no
merge). The dense rows below the DSA's dense limit take the implicit
list 0 .. p. Prompt passes of 64 rows or more at <= 16 heads a rank;
TF_GLM_MSA=0 keeps the chunk kernels. 206 registers, two blocks an SM,
27.6 KB of shared memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
